In this solution, the `search` method uses a binary search approach to find the target value in the rotated sorted array `nums`. The time complexity of the algorithm is O(log n) because the binary search reduces the search space by half in each iteration. The method checks two conditions in each iteration: if the current element `mid` is equal to the target, it returns `mid`. If the left half of the array is sorted (i.e., `nums[mid] >= nums[left]`), it checks if the target is within this range and adjusts the search space accordingly. If the right half of the array is sorted (i.e., `nums[mid] < nums[left]`), it checks if the target is within this range and adjusts the search space accordingly. The loop continues until the target is found or the search space is exhausted.

